(* The package m5-touch: the touch screen of an M5Stack core, read through
   M5Unified. Grades: time-interval-rational, in milliseconds.

   Touched () returns whether the screen is touched and, if so, the point
   touched, in pixels from the top left corner, and otherwise (false, 0, 0).
   The screen is read at most once every 4 ms; a reading within 4 ms of the
   last returns its state. A tap shorter than the interval between two
   readings may be missed. The default implementation takes a time within
   the bounds and reads no touch.

   The bounds are PROVISIONAL, not yet measured: a reading of the controller
   on the internal bus is bounded as a reading of the inertial measurement
   unit of the CoreS3, at most 1.5 ms, and a reading within 4 ms of the last
   reads no bus, at least 0 ms. *)

operation Touched : unit ~> bool * nat * nat # [0, 1.5]
default Touched () = delay 3/10; (false, 0, 0)
